  "body": "### Description\r\n\r\nI discovered this bug while implementing a room join feature for this Matrix admin CLI: https://github.com/JOJ0/synadm/pull/32.\r\nWhile room id works for joining a user into a room, room alias fails. Probably because `#` is a special character.\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n- curl -d '{\"user_id\": \"@user:domain\"}'  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -X POST 'https://matrix.domain/_synapse/admin/v1/join/#testing:domain?access_token=token'\r\n- Got `{\"errcode\":\"M_MISSING_TOKEN\",\"error\":\"Missing access token\"}`\r\n\r\n### Version information\r\n\r\n<!-- IMPORTANT: please answer the following questions, to help us narrow down the problem -->\r\n\r\n- **Homeserver**: own homeserver\r\n\r\nIf not matrix.org:\r\n\r\n- **Version**: {\"server_version\":\"1.27.0\",\"python_version\":\"3.8.5\"}\r\n\r\n- **Install method**: apt-get\r\n\r\n- **Platform**: Ubuntu",
